  "worked_solution": "Given a function of the form $y=A\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{\\pi }{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(\\frac{9x+2\\pi }{3})+4=\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(3x+\\frac{2\\pi }{3})+4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B=3,$ and so the period is $\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$",
